# Money Rule

Never use JavaScript floating-point arithmetic for authoritative money.

Use Prisma Decimal / PostgreSQL NUMERIC or DECIMAL.

This includes invoice totals, tax, discounts, allocations, outstanding, fixed-rate conversion, settlement, refunds, chargebacks, CB/RF, reporting totals, and rounding.

Put formulas in a centralized financial domain layer. Do not duplicate them in React components, Route Handlers, Server Actions, or payment adapters.

Historical fixed-rate snapshots must never be recalculated. Gateway FX must never override Admin-defined rates.

Merchant/processor fees must never change invoice balance, the fixed rate, or converted settlement.

Authoritative docs: `docs/05 Architecture Decisions.md` (ADR-004), `docs/Foundation/Currency and Conversion.md`.
